    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I get it—you're desperate for relief, but even 24 hours at that dose is risky and can cause acute kidney injury or stomach bleeding, especially if you're dehydrated or stressed. The \"short-term\" exception usually means a single dose, not a full day of maxed-out pills. Instead, take 600mg every 6 hours (that's 2,400mg/day, still high but safer) and add a cold pack on the joint for 15 minutes every hour—that will numb it fast while the meds kick in. If you absolutely must push through, drink a lot of water and eat something with the pills to protect your stomach. But honestly, if you're in this much pain, a quick steroid shot from urgent care would get you through the weekend far better than any pill.",
